    "reasoning": "Every field has its own captured worked-solution evidence, and all selected choices agree with that evidence. q-133053: the mean is 4.98912 mm, so the standardized cutoff is about -1.413 and the percentage rounds to 7.9%. q-132860: symmetry gives an upper cumulative probability of 0.97, hence a mean of approximately 4.702 and a standardized cutoff of approximately 0.3973. The supplied-table method rounds this cutoff to 0.40 and gives 65.5%, matching MA. Using greater precision gives approximately 65.4447%; thus 65.5% is a table approximation, rather than the exact percentage rounded to one decimal. The question specifies no required rounding precision. q-164830: the linear terms cancel and the quadratic term is -(1-\\pi/4)^2. q-109090: Var(X)=2/5, so Var(\\sqrt{5}X+4)=5(2/5)=2. q-110220: X^2=9 precisely when X=-3 or X=3, giving 0.35+0.10=0.45. q-148669: Bayes' theorem gives P(S)=0.7(0.03)/0.025=0.84; total probability then gives (0.84-0.23(0.92)-0.41(0.95))/0.36=0.663611..., rounding to 0.664. q-143876: equal basket probabilities give the unknown ripe proportion as 3/4-1/6-1/5=23/60. q-42567: Bayes' theorem gives 0.6(0.4)/0.3=0.8. q-135395: writing A=I+N gives N^2=0, so A^{-1}=I-N. q-130807: multiplying [[1,-8],[0,1]] by [[1,0],[-6,1]] gives [[49,-8],[-6,1]]. q-111083: the union contains cells (0,1), (1,1), (1,2), and (2,1), whose probabilities sum to 0.7. q-96055: differentiating -2 coth(t)+cosh(t) recovers the integrand. q-95505: the chain rule gives e^x/(1-e^{2x}), valid on the real domain x<0. q-42890: determinant-preserving row additions followed by expansion along column 2 give -2(4-3)=-2. q-38540: x has B-coordinates (0,-5), whose image coordinates are (0,-10,-10). q-73257: substituting z=y+3 and completing the square gives (x-2)^2/3+(y+1)^2/4=1/2, equivalent to the selected ellipse. No earlier submitted answer or captured grade was provided; the judgments use the individual worked solutions.",
